---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="That didn't go through · YOLO Electronics Repair"
  description="The repair request form didn't go through. Email YOLO Electronics Repair instead."
>
  <div>
    <h1>That didn't go through</h1>
    <p class="sub">NOTHING WAS SAVED</p>
  </div>
  <p class="tag">Email it instead.</p>
  <p class="note">Send the same details to <a href="mailto:hello@yolorepair.com">hello@yolorepair.com</a>: what it is, what it's doing, and drop-off or mail-in. Email is still the front door.</p>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Or try the form again</h2>
    <p class="note">Going back in your browser usually brings back what you typed. A message that's mostly links gets turned away, and so does a run of requests inside an hour.</p>
    <p class="note"><a href="/request/">Back to the form</a></p>
  </section>
</Base>
